
                    Dark sky, white ground, 
                    Famished eyes all around.

                    Ski the fields, fast as wind, 
                    The pack chases through the glen.

                    In the wood, now in front,
                    Salivating from the hunt.

                    Rigid bodies, snarling fangs,
                    Suddenly, haunches sprang.

                    Flailing poles, naked throat,
                    Running, gaping, crimson moat...

    You awake with a start. The tour bus was snaking its way through 
a long shadowed pass, the countryside below was covered in a snowflake 
blanket, and the only protrudence was the savage range of Styrian 
mountains. 

    Your heart still raced from the dream, those wolves almost... no, 
they HAD you. These "pre-race nerves" weren't usually this severe, then
again, the International May Day race wasn't your usual race, either.

    Suddenly, the bus lurched to a stop and a rap came on the door,
revealing a well bundeled officer wielding a flare. After a quick 
discourse in German with the driver and coach, the officer worked his way
to the next vehicle in line.

    "It seems.." began the coach, "that an avalanche has blocked the 
pass. We'll be returning to a village about 15 kilometers back to stay
for the evening. With any luck they'll have the pass clear by morning,
and we can get to the race site with minimal affect on our schedule.

    A groan emitted from some of the staff and team, but you merely
pulled deeper into your coat and thoughts. It was the reaction of the 
driver however, that caught your thoughts... he had crossed himself 
severely at the news, mumbling something about "Walpurgisnacht" and had, 
if you're not mistaken, argued heatedly with the coach. As he hesitantly
turned the bus about, you pondered the odd superstitions of the locals 
that had made the driver so reluctant to drive this evening. Whatever 
it was, one would have thought that modern science would have stomped 
out such silly beliefs long ago....



