   You find yourself in line at the counter of what you discover is a
chateau-turned-hotel, overlooking the little town of Karnstein. From 
behind the counter, a spectacled woman whose wiry hair seemingly refuses 
to be reigned in by hairpins, greets the group in a thick accent

   "Velcome! Velcome, to Karnstein Chateau. Mein goodness, vee have 
such distinvished guests and dear me, on such an evening. Vell no matter, 
but vee must hurry all of you in here, and close zhose doors." says Oma. 
     Teammates and competitors alike await their turn in line to sign in 
and receive their room key.
   "If you'll excuse me for a moment, I'll prepare zhe kitchen for your 
arrival. Vhen all of your party has signed in, if you vill ring zhe bell, 
I vill return to show you to your rooms." the old woman smiles briefly
and scurries off.
